   "source": [
    "## 3. Class Imbalance Analysis\n",
    "In financial fraud detection, positive (fraudulent) transactions represent a tiny minority of all transactions.\n",
    "- **Why Accuracy Fails:** If 99.8% of transactions are legitimate, a naive classifier that predicts *Legitimate* 100% of the time achieves **99.8% Accuracy**, yet catches **0% of fraud** and incurs catastrophic financial loss.\n",
    "- **Evaluation Mandate:** We must evaluate models using **Precision-Recall AUC (PR-AUC)**, **Recall (Sensitivity)**, **Precision**, and business cost matrices.\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 4,
   "id": "54201c6a",
   "metadata": {
    "execution": {
